What:		/sys/bus/iio/devices/iio:deviceX/out_altvoltage0_band
KernelVersion:
Contact:	linux-iio@vger.kernel.org
Description:
		Read/write the RF output band selection. The ADMV1355 has two
		internal RF signal paths (low band and high band) selected by
		this attribute. No standard IIO attribute maps to internal
		band-path routing.
		Valid values: low_band high_band

What:		/sys/bus/iio/devices/iio:deviceX/out_altvoltage0_band_available
KernelVersion:
Contact:	linux-iio@vger.kernel.org
Description:
		List of available RF band selections.

What:		/sys/bus/iio/devices/iio:deviceX/in_altvoltage0_mode
KernelVersion:
Contact:	linux-iio@vger.kernel.org
Description:
		Read/write the IF input operating mode. The ADMV1355 supports
		four mixer modes with different intermediate frequency input
		configurations. This selects which internal IF path is active.
		No standard IIO channel type covers device-specific mixer mode
		selection.
		Valid values: baseband complex_if_low complex_if_high if_hybrid

What:		/sys/bus/iio/devices/iio:deviceX/in_altvoltage0_mode_available
KernelVersion:
Contact:	linux-iio@vger.kernel.org
Description:
		List of available IF input modes.

What:		/sys/bus/iio/devices/iio:deviceX/in_altvoltage1_sideband
KernelVersion:
Contact:	linux-iio@vger.kernel.org
Description:
		Read/write the mixer sideband selection. Controls whether the
		lower sideband (LSB) or upper sideband (USB) of the mixer
		output is selected. This is a fundamental mixer topology control
		with no standard IIO mapping.
		Valid values: LSB USB

What:		/sys/bus/iio/devices/iio:deviceX/in_altvoltage1_sideband_available
KernelVersion:
Contact:	linux-iio@vger.kernel.org
Description:
		List of available mixer sideband selections.

What:		/sys/bus/iio/devices/iio:deviceX/out_altvoltage0_direct_lpf_val
KernelVersion:
Contact:	linux-iio@vger.kernel.org
Description:
		Read/write the direct-path RF low-pass filter tuning word (4-bit,
		register 0x80B[3:0]). Sets the filter corner frequency for the
		direct RF output path. No standard IIO filter attribute exists.

What:		/sys/bus/iio/devices/iio:deviceX/out_altvoltage0_direct_hpf_val
KernelVersion:
Contact:	linux-iio@vger.kernel.org
Description:
		Read/write the direct-path RF high-pass filter tuning word (4-bit,
		register 0x80B[7:4]).

What:		/sys/bus/iio/devices/iio:deviceX/out_altvoltage0_bypass_lpf_en
KernelVersion:
Contact:	linux-iio@vger.kernel.org
Description:
		Enable/disable the bypass-path LPF (register 0x2A0[4]). When
		enabled, the LPF bypass filter bank is active instead of the
		direct-path LPF.

What:		/sys/bus/iio/devices/iio:deviceX/out_altvoltage0_bypass_lpf_val
KernelVersion:
Contact:	linux-iio@vger.kernel.org
Description:
		Read/write the bypass-path LPF tuning word (4-bit,
		register 0x2A0[3:0]).

What:		/sys/bus/iio/devices/iio:deviceX/out_altvoltage0_bypass_hpf_en
KernelVersion:
Contact:	linux-iio@vger.kernel.org
Description:
		Enable/disable the bypass-path HPF (register 0x2A1[7]). When
		enabled, the HPF bypass filter bank is active instead of the
		direct-path HPF.

What:		/sys/bus/iio/devices/iio:deviceX/out_altvoltage0_bypass_hpf_val
KernelVersion:
Contact:	linux-iio@vger.kernel.org
Description:
		Read/write the bypass-path HPF tuning word (6-bit,
		register 0x2A1[5:0]).

What:		/sys/bus/iio/devices/iio:deviceX/in_altvoltage1_lo_x4_filter
KernelVersion:
Contact:	linux-iio@vger.kernel.org
Description:
		Read/write the LO x4 harmonic-reject filter band selection.
		Normally auto-configured from the LO clock rate. This manual
		override is for custom frequency plans.

What:		/sys/bus/iio/devices/iio:deviceX/in_altvoltage1_lo_x4_filter_available
KernelVersion:
Contact:	linux-iio@vger.kernel.org
Description:
		List of available LO x4 filter selections.

What:		/sys/bus/iio/devices/iio:deviceX/in_altvoltage1_lo_x3_filter
KernelVersion:
Contact:	linux-iio@vger.kernel.org
Description:
		Read/write the LO x3 harmonic-reject filter band selection.

What:		/sys/bus/iio/devices/iio:deviceX/in_altvoltage1_lo_x3_filter_available
KernelVersion:
Contact:	linux-iio@vger.kernel.org
Description:
		List of available LO x3 filter selections.

What:		/sys/bus/iio/devices/iio:deviceX/in_altvoltage1_lo_x1_filter
KernelVersion:
Contact:	linux-iio@vger.kernel.org
Description:
		Read/write the LO x1 harmonic-reject filter band selection.

What:		/sys/bus/iio/devices/iio:deviceX/in_altvoltage1_lo_x1_filter_available
KernelVersion:
Contact:	linux-iio@vger.kernel.org
Description:
		List of available LO x1 filter selections.

What:		/sys/bus/iio/devices/iio:deviceX/in_altvoltage1_lo_trap
KernelVersion:
Contact:	linux-iio@vger.kernel.org
Description:
		Read/write the LO trap filter tuning word (10-bit, 0-1023).
		Internal trap filter used to reject unwanted LO harmonics.

What:		/sys/bus/iio/devices/iio:deviceX/in_altvoltage1_lo_dbl_band
KernelVersion:
Contact:	linux-iio@vger.kernel.org
Description:
		Read/write the LO doubler band tuning word (8-bit, 0-255).
		Controls the internal LO frequency doubler band selection.

What:		/sys/bus/iio/devices/iio:deviceX/gain_lut_bypass_en
KernelVersion:
Contact:	linux-iio@vger.kernel.org
Description:
		Enable/disable the gain LUT bypass mode (register 0x28A[0]).
		When enabled, the DSA bypass channels (out_altvoltage3,
		out_altvoltage4) control attenuation directly instead of the
		main DSA channels, and the gain LUT drives the bypass DSA
		path. This selects an alternate signal routing that has no
		standard IIO equivalent.

What:		/sys/bus/iio/devices/iio:deviceX/direct_gpo_g
KernelVersion:
Contact:	linux-iio@vger.kernel.org
Description:
		Read/write the direct-path GPO G output value (5-bit, 0-31,
		register 0x601). Controls general-purpose output pins used
		for board-level signal routing in the direct signal path.
		No standard IIO GPIO attribute exists for device-internal
		GPO pins tied to signal-path state.

What:		/sys/bus/iio/devices/iio:deviceX/bypass_gpo_g
KernelVersion:
Contact:	linux-iio@vger.kernel.org
Description:
		Read/write the bypass-path GPO G output value (5-bit, 0-31,
		register 0x28C). Controls general-purpose output pins used
		for board-level signal routing in the bypass signal path.

What:		/sys/bus/iio/devices/iio:deviceX/direct_gpo_f
KernelVersion:
Contact:	linux-iio@vger.kernel.org
Description:
		Read/write the direct-path GPO F output value (6-bit, 0-63,
		register 0x803). Controls general-purpose output pins used
		for board-level signal routing in the direct signal path.

What:		/sys/bus/iio/devices/iio:deviceX/gpo_f_oe
KernelVersion:
Contact:	linux-iio@vger.kernel.org
Description:
		Read/write the GPO F output-enable mask (6-bit, 0-63,
		register 0x780[5:0]). Each bit enables the corresponding
		GPO F pin as an output.

What:		/sys/bus/iio/devices/iio:deviceX/gpo_g_oe
KernelVersion:
Contact:	linux-iio@vger.kernel.org
Description:
		Read/write the GPO G output-enable mask (5-bit, 0-31,
		registers 0x780[7:6] and 0x781[2:0]). Each bit enables the
		corresponding GPO G pin as an output.
